{
  "row": {
    "id": 15,
    "scenario": "A crash at each step of design §6's recovery table",
    "required_outcome": "One consistent state, no duplicate"
  },
  "design": ["§6 Write protocol, the mutation table: create / update / archive / confirm (steps 1–4), forget (steps 1–3), and the recovery at service start for each; the workspace-move row is exercised by fixture 17", "§7a control snapshot `pending`"],
  "loads_in": ["slice-2"],
  "notes_for_implementer": "Every `crash_at` runs the mutation up to and including the named step and then drops the service without step 3/4 (the harness injects the stop); `restart` is the recovery at service start. Steps of the create/update row: 1 = `pending` set; 2a = the `.history/<id>/<to_rev>.md` copy written and fsynced, the note not yet renamed into place; 2 = the note written (temp, fsync, rename) and `.history` pruned; 3 = the snapshot records `to_rev` and origin and clears `pending`. Forget: 1 = tombstone appended; 2 = files deleted; 3 = index purged. Each case ends in the state the table's recovery column names; `no duplicate` means the note is listed once (never one entry per revision) and the index agrees with the file. `@from_rev` and `@to_rev` are the interrupted mutation's, which the harness knows because it planned the write. The `pending` object is checked in the §7a shape between crash and restart so the recovery reads exactly what the table says it reads.",
  "owners": [
    { "id": "u_example_alice", "owner_key": "32acea7eb739b08afd959db91e46d450" }
  ],
  "database": { "global_users": ["u_example_alice"], "local_user_id": "u_example_alice" },
